Upstream provenance
-------------------

Zoysh is a zsh port and adaptation of Yosh, created by Fil Pizlo:

    https://github.com/pizlonator/yosh

The original Yosh project introduced the `yo` interaction and the LLM provider,
configuration, session-memory, terminal-awareness, and multi-step designs that
Zoysh adapts for zsh. Yosh's `readline-8.2.13/yo.c` carries this notice:

    Copyright (C) 2026 Epic Games, Inc.

That upstream file is offered under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later. Zoysh's zsh-specific implementation and modifications are Copyright (C)
2026 Stefano Tondo and are distributed under GPL-3.0-only.

The current script-plugin release does not bundle GNU Bash, GNU Readline, or
cJSON. The experimental native-module directory contains zsh module boilerplate;
if future work imports upstream source, contributors must retain the applicable
copyright and license notices.

